        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "8a32894ce6949d07dc9b4b6d9f62497cc8f0d920",
            "parents": [
                "7fb9bb4f60eef821fb3964888a25cbc4e4e54718"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/68/80968/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Shane Lin",
                "email": "hslin@nvidia.com",
                "username": "x86driver"
            },
            "createdOn": 1749541942,
            "author": {
                "name": "Shane Lin",
                "email": "hslin@nvidia.com",
                "username": "x86driver"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm looking at the changes to the per-page semantics and they seem pretty doable.  How hard is it to do sed/automated replace for the changes?  Is there a list of required xml changes somewhere?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net It is very doable to remove the plugin.  However Bootstrap isn't just CSS, it is a javascript library, and in a few instances is not compatible with Vue.  We would have to update all pages that have a select box to not use Bootstrap for select boxes for instance and use pure Vue3 versions.  Same for tooltips and modals."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we focus on https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/82993  ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "+1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we close this PR as we have already migrated to Bootstrap-vue-next in master?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Plan is to move to BootstrapVueNext in Vue3. So. Directly we can Move from BootstrapVue -> BootstrapVueNext which internally uses Bootstrapv5. Instead of moving from BootstrapVue -> Bootstrapv5 -> BootstrapVueNext. \n\nMinimal changes in code."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Through our conversations on the topic, it was determined that the *ideal* was to remove the reliance on a Vue plugin for Bootstrap support.  We came to the conclusion that moving to BootstrapVueNext could be accomplished sooner with significantly less effort.  However, that did not happen in a timely manner.\n\nInternally we already have the entire WebUI moved to Bootstrap 5 in a single MR. However we decided to upstream here just with Overview and include fallback support for all other pages.  This should allow us to thoroughly review this approach and once committed, allow us to quickly update the rest of webui.\n\nThe removal of bootstrap tags and restoration of HTML5 tags in the markup is worth the effort."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "@hslin@nvidia.com , looking at some other display bugs outside of the scope of this patch.. I see issues with dropdowns and some other widgets.  This led me back to this:  https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/javascript/#usage-with-javascript-frameworks\n\nSince we are using Vue3, the bootstrap docs itself prescribes BootstrapVueNext \ud83d\ude02"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "`Since we are using Vue3, the bootstrap docs itself prescribes BootstrapVueNext \ud83d\ude02` \nRight!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "@Nikhil if we can move directly to bootstrap5 with no extra dependency, isn't that more ideal?  BootstrapVueNext likely still has arch issues that we shouldn't really want to solve.  The fewer dependencies we have, the better."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Since we are using Vue as our framework for development, We have considered to use BootstrapVueNext as it is recommended. We have done this in our downstream and did not face any major issues while using BootstrapVueNext. Can you give more information about the arch. issues you mentioned?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Every time bootstrap updates, we hit this problem where the new bootstrap isn't supported for sometimes years in a vue component.  Moving to pure bootstrap would mean that we can upgrade freely.  This lack of support initially stopped the Vue3 upgrade.\n\nIf you want to do BootstrapVueNext, when will patches be put in review?  That's great you did it in your downstream, but that doesn't help upstream."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "I think that this would be an easy decision if Bootstrap 5 was completely compatible with Vue 3.  It is not.\n\nWe can't use pure Bootstrap without issues.  We could use it and then fill the compatibility gaps though, which is really what the plugin does.\n\nWe have seemingly made the decision to stick with both Bootstrap and Vue, and these two libs do not have fully compatible javascript.  The move to Vue 3 requires us to move on from bootstrap-vue.  So either we work around that by creating our own compatibility layers or use something off the shelf that has more momentum.  Using BootstrapVueNext indeed puts us in the same position of depending on a third party plugin and we will have to deal with that going forward, but we would be in the same pickle if we instead hack around the incompatibilities ourselves.  Plus there would be a lot of effort to make that work; Dynamically creating and styling shadow-DOM dropdowns that work across all browsers is no picnic... and really we should be more focused on content.  The pain point would continue to be package versioning in the project."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "To clarify on the downstream patches, these were retained downstream based on a decision we arrived at an earlier community call, where it was decided that the upstream would continue with Vuex and Vue CLI. IBM had proposed moving to the recommended packages (Vite & Pinia). Hence in the IBM downstream, we worked on the migration to Vue3 using Vite and Pinia, rather than adopting the migration build path. \n\nHowever, we have been engaged in supporting for any upstream reviews. In downstream, we have completed about 95% of the migration work and haven't seen any issues with the Vue3 + BootstrapVueNext combination.\n\nGiven that the migration in upstream hasn't progressed much, we can now start exploring contributing our BootstrapVueNext implementation back to the community.\n\nAlso, I agree with Jason that BootstrapVueNext provides a much more convenient approach compared to using Bootstrap alone."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": ">  a decision we arrived at an earlier community call, where it was decided that the upstream would continue with Vuex and Vue CLI. \n\nLet's be sure to talk about this Thursday.\nI was not aware of the desire to keep Vuex and Vue CLI as both of those are deprecated.  \nI would hope that the plan is to update to Vite and Pinia, but in separate patches, perhaps once the Bootstrap 5 migration is complete.\nAs to BS5, we will close this CR as it is incorporated into 82993."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, We can talk about this. We had 2 PRs initially: ( https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/55438 and https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/67959 ). Because in Upstream, the desire was to complete faster and with minimal changes, Vuex and Vue CLI was decided. But in our downstream, we had chosen Vite and Pinia as the former was deprecated. Hence had to part ways between upstream and downstream for this migration. Yes, We should consider to move to latter packages."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "We must address this.  We are at a point where everyone using this project has a massively diverged downstream (myself included).  Let's fix it!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> an earlier community call, where it was decided that the upstream would continue with Vuex and Vue CLI\n\nTo reiterate the rules regarding community calls;  Because they only include a subset of the interested members, they can make no \"decisions\", they can only help to drive consensus to the mailing list, gerrit, or discord.  I'm hoping that's just a typo."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/Login/Login.vue",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the input @ed@tanous.net.\n\nAgree with `no \"decisions\"`\n\nRephased: \nTo clarify on the downstream patches, these were retained downstream because we were using Vite and Pinia. In an earlier community call, we arrived at a majority consensus that the upstream would continue with Vuex and Vue CLI.However, IBM had proposed moving to the recommended packages (Vite & Pinia). Hence in the IBM downstream, we worked on the migration to Vue3 using Vite and Pinia, rather than adopting the migration build path."
                }
